    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests the Simplified Soundex variant ({@link Soundex#US_ENGLISH_SIMPLIFIED}). In this mode H and W are treated the same as vowels: they are not encoded but they <em>do</em> act as separators between consecutive consonants that share the same code group. <p> Algorithm rules from: http://west-penwith.org.uk/misc/soundex.htm </p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "i39",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     439,
     439
    ],
    "own_line": false,
    "norm": "treat vowels and HW as separators"
   },
   {
    "id": "i40",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     446,
     447
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "In Simplified mode 'o', 'w', and 'h' all act as separators, so the duplicate D's in \"Dodds\" are split and each contributes its own code."
   },
   {
    "id": "i41",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     449,
     449
    ],
    "own_line": false,
    "norm": "w is a separator"
   },
   {
    "id": "i42",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     450,
     450
    ],
    "own_line": false,
    "norm": "h is a separator"
   },
   {
    "id": "i43",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     453,
     461
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests the Genealogy Soundex variant ({@link Soundex#US_ENGLISH_GENEALOGY}). In this mode vowels (A, E, I, O, U, Y), H, and W are all completely silent: they are ignored after the first character and do <em>not</em> act as separators between duplicate codes. <p> Algorithm rules from: http://www.genealogy.com/articles/research/00000060.html </p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "i44",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     463,
     463
    ],
    "own_line": false,
    "norm": "treat vowels and HW as silent"
   },
   {
    "id": "i45",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     469,
     470
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "In Genealogy mode 'o', 'h', and 'w' are all silent (not separators), so each pair of D's collapses to a single code-3 slot."
   },
   {
    "id": "i46",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     471,
     471
    ],
    "own_line": false,
    "norm": "'o' is not a separator here - it is silent"
   },
   {
    "id": "i47",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     472,
     472
    ],
    "own_line": false,
    "norm": "'h' is silent"
   },
   {
    "id": "i48",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     473,
     473
    ],
    "own_line": false,
    "norm": "'w' is silent"
   },
   {
    "id": "i49",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     476,
     478
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "----------------------------------------------------------------------- Phonetic difference score -----------------------------------------------------------------------"
   },
   {
    "id": "i50",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     480,
     484
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link Soundex#difference(String, String)}, which counts how many character positions match between two Soundex codes and returns a score from 0 (no phonetic similarity) to 4 (identical phonetics)."
